            <div xml:id="d821">

                <pb facs="1288" n="1274" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1274"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 European War/1258: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-27T17:00:00-04:00">January 27, 1944—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>673. For Pell. The Department has no objection to allowing Mr. Preuss to act as
                    alternate at meetings of Commission as suggested your 514, January 19.</p>
                <pb facs="1289" n="1275" xml:id="pg1275"/>
                <p>Matter of dropping technical committee has not been brought to Department’s
                    attention by the British Government. Your detailed report not yet received.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
